WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.920 --> 00:00:05.760
Did you ever wonder if certain foods
have a direct effect on your health?

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:07.720
Well, I’m here to
solve that mystery

00:00:07.720 --> 00:00:11.200
since you are
the foods you eat.

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:13.280
Welcome to the
Nutrition Facts Podcast.

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:16.120
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:16.120 --> 00:00:19.600
Today, it’s part two of our
series on fluoride in water.

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:24.920
And we’ll start with some new research
that helped me change my own mind

00:00:24.920 --> 00:00:27.800
about the safety of fluoridation.

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:29.720
Community water fluoridation
recently hit

00:00:29.720 --> 00:00:31.400
its 75th anniversary,

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:35.040
touted as a significant
advancement in public health,

00:00:35.040 --> 00:00:36.840
but new research
suggests the potential

00:00:36.840 --> 00:00:39.560
for adverse health impacts.

00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:41.560
There's little question
that supplemental fluoride

00:00:41.560 --> 00:00:43.840
strengthens teeth
and reduces decay.

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:45.600
But at what cost?

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:48.280
Most of the older studies
were snapshot-in-time studies,

00:00:48.280 --> 00:00:50.240
looking only at group-level data

00:00:50.240 --> 00:00:53.280
or were based on
higher-than-normal exposure.

00:00:53.280 --> 00:00:55.480
That has since changed
with the publication

00:00:55.480 --> 00:00:56.840
of prospective studies

00:00:56.840 --> 00:00:59.040
following individual
exposure levels from

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:01.760
mother-child pairs over time.

00:01:01.760 --> 00:01:03.800
The first few were from Mexico

00:01:03.800 --> 00:01:05.520
and correlated
higher fluoride levels

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:07.320
in the urine of pregnant women

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:10.160
with future developmental delay
in their infants.

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:12.240
They found worse cognitive
performance at age four

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:15.000
and lower IQ
from ages six through 12,

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.120
but the fluoride was
from fluoridated salt

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:20.640
or water sources where fluoride
was present naturally.

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:23.200
Then, this study
came out of Canada,

00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:26.720
the first prospective study
using individual exposure data

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:30.480
dealing directly with
community water fluoridation

00:01:30.480 --> 00:01:31.880
receiving quote-unquote

00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:34.520
"optimally fluoridated" water.

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:36.400
None of the municipal
water fluoride levels

00:01:36.400 --> 00:01:38.440
exceeded 1.5 parts per million,

00:01:38.440 --> 00:01:40.520
and the vast majority,
over 90 percent,

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:43.960
were under the U.S.
target of point seven.

00:01:43.960 --> 00:01:46.720
Despite drinking
"optimally fluoridated water,"

00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:49.840
the study of more than
500 mother-child pairs

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:52.160
found that higher fluoride
exposure during pregnancy,

00:01:52.160 --> 00:01:54.440
once again,
appeared to translate

00:01:54.440 --> 00:01:59.320
into lower child intelligence,
measured at ages three to four.

00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:01.680
The American College of
Obstetricians and Gynecologists

00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:03.400
recommends pregnant women drink

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:05.200
at least eight cups
of water a day.

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:07.000
Based on the Canadian study,

00:02:07.000 --> 00:02:07.960
following this advice

00:02:07.960 --> 00:02:10.560
with water at U.S.
target fluoridation levels

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:14.360
might result in as much as
a 5-point loss in IQ.

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:16.200
The Canadian study was published

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:18.440
in the American
Medical Association's

00:02:18.440 --> 00:02:19.560
pediatrics journal,

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:22.440
the longest running pediatrics
journal in the country.

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:25.840
The editor-in-chief defended its
decision to publish the study

00:02:26.720 --> 00:02:30.600
"as testament to the fact that
JAMA Pediatrics is committed

00:02:30.600 --> 00:02:32.960
to disseminating
the best science...

00:02:32.960 --> 00:02:36.200
regardless of how contentious
the results may be."

00:02:37.440 --> 00:02:38.560
The Canadian Agency

00:02:38.560 --> 00:02:40.120
for Drugs and Technologies
in Health

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:42.080
issued a rapid response report,

00:02:42.080 --> 00:02:44.480
concluding that there
is insufficient evidence

00:02:44.480 --> 00:02:47.680
to conclusively conclude
that fluoride exposure

00:02:47.680 --> 00:02:50.640
at optimum levels affects
neurological development,

00:02:50.640 --> 00:02:54.200
but that's not what
the Canadian study was saying.

00:02:54.200 --> 00:02:56.760
The researchers just suggested
the "possible need"

00:02:56.760 --> 00:02:59.240
to reduce fluoride intake
during pregnancy.

00:02:59.240 --> 00:03:01.160
As the accompanying
editorial concluded,

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:02.520
based on the new data,

00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:04.800
"a dispassionate
and tempered discussion

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:09.200
of fluoride's potential
neurotoxicity is warranted."

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:12.560
What was the response
from US regulators?

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:14.960
Within a month of
the Canadian study's release,

00:03:14.960 --> 00:03:17.520
the National Toxicology Program,

00:03:17.520 --> 00:03:18.840
which is part
of the US Department

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:19.880
of Health and Human Services

00:03:19.880 --> 00:03:21.720
that evaluates substances

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:23.880
for potentially harmful
human health effects,

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:26.760
released a draft evaluation
of fluoride exposure

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:29.320
and neurodevelopmental
and cognitive health effects

00:03:29.320 --> 00:03:30.160
and concluded that,

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:34.040
"Based on a systematic review
of the evidence,

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:38.200
the NTP concludes that
fluoride is presumed to be

00:03:38.200 --> 00:03:41.960
a cognitive neurodevelopmental
hazard to humans."

00:03:43.600 --> 00:03:45.800
So we've gone
from dismissing people

00:03:45.800 --> 00:03:47.600
who questioned the safety
of water fluoridation

00:03:47.600 --> 00:03:50.240
as zealots
or anti-science fanatics,

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:53.640
to the official US National
Toxicology Program saying

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:56.520
we should presume
it's hazardous.

00:03:56.520 --> 00:03:58.800
Now, this was just
a draft report.

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:00.840
To ensure the integrity
of its report,

00:04:00.840 --> 00:04:02.800
the NTP asked
the National Academies,

00:04:02.800 --> 00:04:05.160
probably our most prestigious
scientific institution,

00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:06.520
to review it.

00:04:06.520 --> 00:04:08.680
The review raised
a bunch of concerns,

00:04:08.680 --> 00:04:11.240
which was portrayed
in the dental literature

00:04:11.240 --> 00:04:13.800
as "discrediting"
the IQ research.

00:04:13.800 --> 00:04:16.720
But that's not what
the National Academies said.

00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:19.480
They explicitly said that
their misgivings don't mean

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:20.680
that the NTP conclusion

00:04:20.680 --> 00:04:24.360
that fluoride should be presumed
to be neurotoxic is incorrect;

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:26.680
they just wanted
some further analysis.

00:04:26.680 --> 00:04:29.760
So, in 2020,
they redrafted their draft,

00:04:29.760 --> 00:04:32.280
and once again came
to the same conclusion,

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:35.080
presuming it's a cognitive
neurodevelopmental hazard

00:04:35.080 --> 00:04:37.480
based on the extent,
consistency,

00:04:37.480 --> 00:04:40.400
and robustness of the IQ data.

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:41.320
The National Academies

00:04:41.320 --> 00:04:43.760
then rereviewed
their redrafted draft,

00:04:43.760 --> 00:04:45.280
concluding it's much improved,

00:04:45.280 --> 00:04:47.320
but urged the NTP
to further improve

00:04:47.320 --> 00:04:48.560
the clarity of the document,

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:52.640
and we await
the final NTP report.

00:04:52.640 --> 00:04:53.680
In our final story,

00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:59.360
we look at medicine’s response to the
changing science on fluoride safety.

00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:01.000
The National Toxicology Program

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:02.640
is part of the
Public Health Service,

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:05.800
in partnership with
the CDC, FDA, and NIH,

00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:08.160
dedicated to the analysis
of agents of concern

00:05:08.160 --> 00:05:11.240
to identify any toxic effects.

00:05:11.240 --> 00:05:14.260
How did the medical community
respond to the draft conclusions

00:05:14.260 --> 00:05:17.120
in their recent systematic
review that concluded that

00:05:17.120 --> 00:05:21.160
fluoride is to be presumed to be
a cognitive neurodevelopmental

00:05:21.160 --> 00:05:22.520
hazard to humans,

00:05:22.520 --> 00:05:24.720
based on studies
showing lower IQ scores

00:05:24.720 --> 00:05:27.680
among kids with
higher fluoride exposure?

00:05:27.680 --> 00:05:30.080
What do you do
when current research

00:05:30.080 --> 00:05:32.040
contradicts public practices,

00:05:32.040 --> 00:05:36.240
when new evidence doesn't
conform with existing beliefs?

00:05:36.240 --> 00:05:38.520
Well, health authorities
have continued to conclude

00:05:38.520 --> 00:05:41.200
that fluoride is
unequivocally safe,

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:42.800
despite the new studies
in recent years

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:44.480
linking fluoride
exposure in pregnancy

00:05:44.480 --> 00:05:47.200
with adverse effects
on fetal brain development.

00:05:47.200 --> 00:05:49.480
There are still papers
on how to "sell"

00:05:49.480 --> 00:05:51.280
fluoridation
of the water supply,

00:05:51.280 --> 00:05:52.440
targeting social media

00:05:52.440 --> 00:05:55.720
and the person-to-person spread
of fluoride "misinformation."

00:05:55.720 --> 00:05:58.200
Search engines are to be
encouraged, at the very least,

00:05:58.200 --> 00:06:00.040
to flag search engine results

00:06:00.040 --> 00:06:03.000
that point to water fluoridation
health "misinformation"

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:04.920
suggesting adverse effects.

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:07.600
In promoting support for
community water fluoridation,

00:06:07.600 --> 00:06:09.880
maybe we don't even want
to proclaim its safety

00:06:09.880 --> 00:06:12.400
for fear of raising
questions about risks.

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:14.240
I mean, if you're
saying it's safe,

00:06:14.240 --> 00:06:17.160
then that begs the question,
"Well, is it not safe?"

00:06:17.160 --> 00:06:20.440
Maybe we shouldn't even
talk about whether it's safe.

00:06:20.440 --> 00:06:22.640
The tendency
to ignore new evidence

00:06:22.640 --> 00:06:25.040
that does not conform
to widespread beliefs

00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:27.720
may be impeding
our response to early warnings

00:06:27.720 --> 00:06:30.720
about fluoride as a potential
developmental neurotoxin,

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:32.480
but some are just so
fixed in their views

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:35.120
on fluoridation that they
won't reassess their stance

00:06:35.120 --> 00:06:38.280
no matter what
the latest research might show.

00:06:38.280 --> 00:06:41.280
Ironically, it was
the antifluoridationists

00:06:41.280 --> 00:06:44.280
who were accused of their
"anti-scientific attitudes,"

00:06:44.280 --> 00:06:47.000
but now it's the
pro-fluoridationists.

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:49.400
One of the most facile
pro-fluoridation arguments

00:06:49.400 --> 00:06:50.920
I ran across is the suggestion

00:06:50.920 --> 00:06:53.280
that fluoride
can't be hurting IQs,

00:06:53.280 --> 00:06:55.240
because over the last
half century of fluoridation,

00:06:55.240 --> 00:06:59.200
IQ scores have been going up
rather than down.

00:06:59.200 --> 00:07:02.800
The jaw-dropping irony is that

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:05.160
a substantial part
of that rise may have been due

00:07:05.160 --> 00:07:09.520
to the removal of another
neurotoxic element, lead.

00:07:09.520 --> 00:07:10.520
It's worth remembering

00:07:10.520 --> 00:07:13.240
that the science surrounding
the neurodevelopmental hazard

00:07:13.240 --> 00:07:16.200
of low-level lead exposure
was also bitterly contested

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:19.200
using the same kinds
of arguments we see today

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:21.000
in the fluoridation debate.

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:22.880
A few short years
before leaded gas

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:25.080
was effectively banned
in the United States,

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:27.880
a meta-analysis of
lead exposure and child IQ

00:07:27.880 --> 00:07:31.280
only found 24 human studies,
all cross-sectional,

00:07:31.280 --> 00:07:33.600
with a typical associated
loss in intelligence

00:07:33.600 --> 00:07:36.320
of about four IQ points.

00:07:36.320 --> 00:07:39.240
The current data suggest
a similar IQ loss from fluoride

00:07:39.240 --> 00:07:42.360
from an even stronger
body of evidence.

00:07:42.360 --> 00:07:44.720
A spokesperson for
the American Dental Association

00:07:44.720 --> 00:07:47.280
responded to the new data
by pointing out

00:07:47.280 --> 00:07:49.720
that some cities that
have ended water fluoridation

00:07:49.720 --> 00:07:52.280
saw an increase in cavities.

00:07:52.280 --> 00:07:54.840
Okay, but that's kind
of a strange response

00:07:54.840 --> 00:07:56.520
to data suggesting the potential

00:07:56.520 --> 00:07:59.600
for permanent brain damage
in children.

00:07:59.600 --> 00:08:02.520
I mean, I know they are
the dental association,

00:08:02.520 --> 00:08:05.480
but how could they so easily
ignore the serious red flags

00:08:05.480 --> 00:08:09.280
of potential neurotoxicity
for cavity reduction?

00:08:09.280 --> 00:08:12.480
This is not to say tooth decay
isn't a serious health issue,

00:08:12.480 --> 00:08:14.920
but there are ways to get the
cavity-preventing benefits

00:08:14.920 --> 00:08:17.360
of fluoride without the risks.

00:08:17.360 --> 00:08:19.240
Since the primary benefits arise

00:08:19.240 --> 00:08:21.560
from topical contact
with our enamel,

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:25.160
but the primary risks arise
from systemic absorption,

00:08:25.160 --> 00:08:28.400
we can follow Europe's example
and safely reap the rewards

00:08:28.400 --> 00:08:31.400
using fluoride toothpaste
and mouthwashes.

00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:33.920
In Europe, 98 percent
of the population

00:08:33.920 --> 00:08:35.920
drink unfluoridated water.

00:08:35.920 --> 00:08:37.760
Several countries,
including France, Germany,

00:08:37.760 --> 00:08:40.400
the Netherlands, Denmark,
Sweden, banned fluoridation

00:08:40.400 --> 00:08:43.320
decades ago in favor
of fluoride toothpaste,

00:08:43.320 --> 00:08:44.600
as more than ten years ago,

00:08:44.600 --> 00:08:46.640
the official scientific
committee on health risks

00:08:46.640 --> 00:08:49.840
of the European Union concluded
that topical application

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:52.560
of fluoride is most effective
in preventing tooth decay

00:08:52.560 --> 00:08:54.520
and that there appears to be
no obvious advantage

00:08:54.520 --> 00:08:58.046
in favor of fluoridating
the water supply.

00:08:58.160 --> 00:09:00.320
We would love it if you could
share with us your stories

00:09:00.320 --> 00:09:03.760
about reinventing your health
through evidence-based nutrition.

00:09:03.760 --> 00:09:06.480
Go to nutritionfacts.org/testimonials.

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:10.640
We may share it on our social
media to help inspire others.

00:09:10.640 --> 00:09:14.560
To see any graphs, charts, graphics,
images, or studies mentioned here,

00:09:14.560 --> 00:09:18.080
please go to the Nutrition Facts
